of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 AUG 94 at 07 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  firm  yellow tan fibrofatty tissue with a wire and x ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal multiple 0 05cm tan  pale calcifications and fibrosis  Sections with calcifications submitted in cassettes A through C  remaining tissue is submitted entirely in cassettes D through F  Resident  FANG FANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST MASS   NO GROSSLY EVIDENT MALIGNANT TUMOR  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST MASS   report_end  , No.
