 a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fibrofatty breast tissue fragment  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm white firm  ill defined nodule present at an inked margin  Representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the specimen submitted in its entirety in cassettes A through D  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
