y focal areas of fat necrosis  This area is 3 6cm from the posterior margin  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm ill defined pink to white fibrotic area  subjacent to the aforementioned erythematous area on the skin  3 0cm inferior to the biopsy cavity  and 5 0cm from the posterior margin  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm ill defined  partially stellate  firm fibrotic area  1 7cm lateral to the biopsy cavity and 3 0cm from the posterior margin  and 1 0cm from the aforementioned fibrotic area  Altogether  these lesions span at least 7cm of breast parenchyma  The uninvolved breast parenchyma consists of primarily unremarkable  lobulated yellow adipose tissue admixed with a scant amount of unremarkable pink white fibrous tissue  The axillary tissue is dissected to reveal multiple rubbery to firm lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE The cut surfaces range from homogeneous and tan white to mottled and tan white to gray  Representative sections are submitted as follows  B F  Biopsy cavity  G H  Ill defined fibrous area subjacent to erythematous skin  I K  Second ill defined fibrotic area and closest posterior margin  L M  Sections through erythematous skin  N  Section through nipple  O  Section through skin with scar  P Q  Representative sections of uninvolved parenchyma  R  Individual intact nodes  S U  One bisected node in each cassette  V  One node trisected  W  One node serially sectioned  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary lymph node  are 3 irregular  firm to soft portions of yellow adipose tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  which are submitted in toto in cassette X  Gross Description by  BETH A  WOODWARD Resident  DAVID COON  PhD  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL  POSITIVE FOR