Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 38 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer on FNA outside hospital  reviewed at MGH                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENSIVELY INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND EXTENDING TO THE POSTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT AND FOCALLY TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE ANTERIOR  SUPERIOR  AND MEDIAL MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND TO THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN    EXCISION  UNREMARKABLE FAT  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLARY NODES   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 09                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  A FEW TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 20     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  number and  left breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE lumpectomy specimen  inked as follows  black deep end superficial  red superior  medial green  lateral blue  inferior yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm white mass grossly abutting the superficial and deep margins  Tumor and adjacent superficial margin are frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Tumor and adjacent deep margin is frozen as FX 2  FX 2 is submitted in cassette A  Section Code  B  tumor with superficial  deep and inferior yellow margin  superficial and is fatty   C  Anterior and deep tissue   superficial fatty   D  Tumor  superior  E  most lateral tissue  radial  F  Most medial tissue  radial  G  firm tissue  inferior  Labeled  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE in aggregate mass of adipose tissue and lymph nodes  submitted in cassettes H L  Labeled  additional left axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm aggregate mass of adipose tissue and tiny lymph nodes measuring less than 0 3cm each  Tissue submitted entirely in cassettes M N  Labeled  left breast additional superficial margin  is a nonoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of breast tissue cauterized on one aspect  submitted completely in cassette O  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1 AND  2  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA WITHIN A FRACTION OF A MILLIMETER FROM INKED SURFACE  MARGINS NEGATIVE  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  Irene Kuter  M D  Eugene Francis Ruffolo  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST  EXCISION PART B  LEFT BREAST  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN PART C  LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES PART D  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 14 CLINICAL DATA  Patient has a history of large infiltrating lobular carcinoma  receptors already done   who now presents for a right modified radical mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  EXTENSIVE  WITH MICROMETASTASIS IN 1 OF 23 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  ALL RESECTION MARGINS ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  2  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FEW FOCI  3  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  FEW FOCI  4  FIBROCYSTIC DISEASE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  5  FIBROADENOMAS  SEVERAL  MICROSCOPIC  6  SKIN OF NIPPLE WITH SEBACEOUS HYPERPLASIA  7  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FIBROSIS  GRANULATION TISSUE  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  AND HISTIOCYTES  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 01 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a 333 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm right mastectomy specimen  which includes a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm right axillary tail  and which is partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm skin ellipse  The specimen is oriented with lateral and superior stitches  The skin ellipse includes a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm areolar with a 3 5cm in length well healed scar that curves along the superior aspect of the areolar  The skin is diffusely tan white and otherwise unremarkable  The deep resection margin is a smooth plane  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a prior REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm cystic biopsy cavity lined by red tan grumose material  and surrounded by a rim of intense fibrosis and semi firm  sulphur yellow discoloration  The biopsy site is 1 0cm subjacent to the epidermal scar  and approaches to within 1 6cm of the deep inked margin  2 0cm of the superior margin  4 0cm of the inferior margin  4 5cm of the lateral margin  and 4 5cm of the medial margin  An extensive and poorly delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm diffuse sheet of firm  gritty  bulging  tan white tissue encroaches upon the biopsy cavity  and extends to within 0 1cm of the deep inked margin  0 1cm of the inferior margin  1 3cm of the superior margin  2 0cm of the lateral margin  and 2 0cm of the medial margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of mature  lobular  yellow  adipose tissue with intercalating fibrous bands  The axillary tail is explored for lymph nodes  twenty three nodes are identified  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right axillary breast node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm lymph node  The tissue is submitted in S  Summary section  AandB  Biopsy cavity and deep inked margin CandD  Biopsy cavity and skin E  Deep inked margin F H  Inferior margin I K  Superior margin L  Lateral margin M  Medial margin N  Nipple O S  Lymph nodes  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA    report_end  , Yes.
