l  and a short suture designating the superior aspect  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior black  the superior green and the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4 cm defect with hemorrhagic borders  consistent with a possible previous biopsy site  Abutting the hemorrhagic border of the cavity is a rubbery to indurated  ill defined tan white nodule  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  this nodule abuts the anterior margin  comes to 0 3cm from the posterior  0 5cm from the superior  REMOVED_DATE from the inferior  0 8cm from the medial and 0 2cm from the lateral margin  respectively  The remainder of the parenchyma is dense  fibrotic and unremarkable tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   medial margin taken en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   uninvolved parenchyma adjacent to medial margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative section of possible cavity and adjacent mass nodule to include all margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   lateral margin taken radially  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and left breast nipple  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3 cm tan pink  focally hemorrhagic  rubbery portion of fibrofatty tissue  There is a suture along one aspect which is designating the new margin  the new sutured margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and left breast inferior medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2 cm tan  yellow  lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue  There is a suture along one aspect designating the new margin  The new margin is inked black  the specimen serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name